# Review policy

How to review changes in this repository. It applies to every reviewer, human or AI.

## Team rules

- Always run `make check` before merging; it is the gate CI uses.
- Database changes need two approvals from the data team.

## What matters in this repo

- `make check` must pass before merge; it runs `make test` and the linter.
- Dispatch behaviour in `src/app.py`: unknown input must stay on the safe path.

## Raise to review even if small

- Database changes (two approvals required; see Team rules).
- Any new event type wired into `src/app.py`.

## Block until a human looks

- A removed or weakened permission or authentication check.
- Changes to how malformed or unhandled input is treated.

## Ignore

- Formatting and import order: the linter owns those; never report them.
- Test data churn in `tests/`.

## Security expectations

- Validate event payloads at the boundary before dispatch.
- Credentials belong in the environment; never commit keys or `.env*` files.

## Evidence and nits

- Every finding names the file and line and quotes the changed code.
- At most 3 nits per PR.
